    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "When you visit a new place, traffic signs are very helpful. It’s hard to imagine a world without traffic signs. You may want to ask: When were traffic signs invented?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "It may sound strange, but the first road signs were "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "milestones",
            "ref": "v-milestone"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". They were used in ancient Rome. Back then, ancient Romans travelled on "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "horseback",
            "ref": "v-horseback"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " or on foot. Milestones were placed every few kilometres. The milestones let travellers know how far they were from Rome."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "After cars were invented, signs became more and more important. Drivers would get lost without signs. "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "As a result",
            "ref": "v-as-a-result"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", Americans began to place signs on busy roads. Early signs were made of wood and were placed on iron "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "columns",
            "ref": "v-column"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". In the 1920s, Americans made the first "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "manual",
            "ref": "v-manual"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " for traffic signs. The book showed what each sign meant. Now, different countries have different traffic sign manuals."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The need for new traffic signs is always growing and changing. In the future, signs may be different, but their goal will not change. Traffic signs will still need to be able to tell people what to do on the road quickly."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      }
    ]
  },
